/**
 * Item-location randomisation — `Rando_randomize_items.gml` and its four helpers
 * (`_1`, `_1a`, `_1a_1`, `_2`). The placement primitives it drives live in `placement.ts`.
 *
 * Shape of the algorithm (ZALiA's own phase comments kept below):
 *  0. build the item pools — A: progression, B: everything else, C = shuffled copy of B;
 *     `dl_prog1` = shuffled copy of A; `dl_locations_remaining` = shuffled item/pbag/key locations.
 *  1. `Rando_randomize_items_1a` opens a route out of the starting area (and to Mido harbour for the RAFT).
 *  2. place progression items, one per pass, always into a location that *adds* new reachable locations,
 *     sweeping spells/skills/keys after each one.
 *  3. place the remaining keys, then everything left, containers first.
 *
 * Dropped as dead code (PORTING.md rule 8): `Rando_randomize_items.gml:65-148` (comment blocks incl. the
 * "proposed required container count" table), `:149-236` (`if (0)` spell-cost clamp experiment),
 * `:410-414`, the unused `var _dm = ds_map_create()` at `:29`; `Rando_randomize_items_1.gml:117-129`
 * (`if (0)` early container placement), `:258-263`, `:494-500` (`if (0)`), `:616-643` (SafeLocation block).
 */
