/**
 * Smasher traps — ZALiA `game_object/gob/gob1/various`: `SmasherTrap01` (a wall/block that waits for the PC
 * to step on its trigger, tells for a moment, then accelerates along one axis until it hits a solid, another
 * SmasherTrap, or the room edge — crushing the PC against whatever is behind them) and `SmasherTrapManager`
 * (an unused conductor that would build a row of traps from one spawn entry and release them together).
 *
 * Both objects are `GOB2` (`SmasherTrap01`'s direct parent is the abstract `SmasherTrap`); all three .gmx
 * event lists are empty, so every behaviour is in the data-bound scripts registered below.
 *
 * `SmasherTrapManager` is dead weight in ZALiA: nothing calls `data_spawn(..., SmasherTrapManager, ...)` and
 * the only step site (`g_Step_A2.gml:89`) is commented out. It is ported because `GameObjectData_Create.gml`
 * still registers its five script slots.
 *
 * Dropped: the `DEBUG1` / `show_debug_message` blocks, the commented-out "change tiles to solid" loops, the
 * commented-out ease-in variant of `SmasherTrap01_update_ATTACK`, and the two `*_end` scripts (they only free
 * ds_grids and surfaces, are not wired to a `data_go_scr` slot, and have nothing to do here).
 */
