/**
 * `Rando_randomize_dungeon_tilesets()` — dungeon tileset rando.
 *
 * Writes two datakey families into `self.dm_save_data_dungeon_tileset` (persisted by
 * `Rando_randomize_file` to `SaveFile_N_RandoDungeonTilesetData.txt` → `f.dm_rando_dungeon_tileset`):
 *  - `_Rando_Tileset_<ts name>` → the tileset each of the seven dungeon tilesets is swapped for.
 *    `scene_enter_add_tiles` reads it back for every `_Dungeon*` tile of a dungeon scene.
 *  - `_WallStyle01<file stem>` / `_WallStyle02<file stem>` → a `ds_grid_write` of per-cell
 *    `tileset index<<8 | tsrc` overrides for one randomly chosen palace, plus a
 *    `_WallStyle0N<file stem><layer name>` marker per layer that carried wall tiles.
 *
 * INERT AS SHIPPED: the wall-style/tile half is only consumed when `_CAN_USE_RANDOMIZED_TILES` is true, and
 * `scene_enter_add_tiles.gml:83` hard-codes it false ("2025/08/11. Turning this off for now. Doesn't look
 * good.", also noted at `Rando_randomize_dungeon_tilesets.gml:87`); the port keeps that constant false in
 * `tile/sceneTiles.ts` too. The `_Rando_Tileset_*` swaps still apply whenever
 * `global.RandoDungeonTilesets_enabled` is on. The code path is ported faithfully regardless.
 *
 * Tiled files: ZALiA reads `rm_tile_data/<Area>/<Area>_NNN.json` with `file_text_open_read` +
 * `json_decode`. Here maps are already parsed and live in `world.maps` (the `MapStore` keyed by file stem
 * that `rm_get_file_data` reads from), so `world.maps.get(stem)` replaces the open/read/decode; a map that
 * is not in the store is GML's `!file_exists(...)` and is skipped, never thrown. In practice the scan never
 * needs a map: `global.dm_scene_wall_data` ships a pre-baked `<stem>_Wall_Part_Data` grid for every palace
 * scene (`set_rm_data_1a` produced them), and that fast path is taken first.
 *
 * Dropped `/* *\/` dead blocks: 87-154 (the `TilesetData01.txt` per-tile shuffle, disabled 2025/08/11),
 * 367-370 and 630-633 (an alternative `_wall_type_data_was_set` latch), 838-934 (an older WallStyle02
 * block-part table driven by `STR_Style`/variation counts). Dead locals `_ts_name`, `_num`, `_idx`,
 * `_dungeon_num` are dropped too; `_ts_name` is assigned in both scan loops but never read.
 */
