/**
 * Location table — `Rando_add_location.gml` and `Rando_init_location_data.gml`.
 *
 * `Rando_init_location_data` is ~2000 lines of straight-line `Rando_add_location()` calls, each followed by
 * its ALLKEY rating and its hint strings. The calls are ported as one `readonly` table walked in the exact
 * source order, because a location's number is `ds_list_size(dl_location_NUMS)+1` — reordering the table
 * renumbers every location after it. Everything that is not a plain row (the `QUEST_NUM` guards, the
 * `FallingKey_RM_NAME` assignment, the trailing `*_COUNT` bookkeeping and the `g.dm_spawn` sweep that finds
 * each location's vanilla spawn datakey / item id) stays real code, in the same sequence.
 *
 * Dropped, all dead in ZALiA:
 * - Commented-out block-comment sections at `Rando_init_location_data.gml:820-823` (a `switch(QUEST_NUM)`
 *   1UP/PBag variant of the JUMP spell room), `:1852-1873` (an older spell-location block with an extra
 *   argument) and `:2079-2175` (a listing of every hint string, kept by the author as a reference sheet).
 * - `if(0)` blocks at `:1977-2033` (print locations grouped by obscurity) and `:2040-2064` (print
 *   `dl_ITEMS`/`dl_PBAGS`/`dl_KEYS`) — both `sdm`-only.
 * - `if (DEBUG){ sdm(…) }` at `:1904-1907` and the `if (DEV …) sdm(…)` warning at
 *   `Rando_add_location.gml:77`: console-only, nothing reaches `dm_debug_data`.
 * - `ds_list_destroy` of the two local scene lists (`:2069-2070`) — the port relies on GC.
 */
