/**
 * `Rando_is_qual_location(location id, *item exception)` and `Rando_is_qual_location_1a()`.
 *
 * "Is this location qualified?" — with the items/spells/skills/keys placed so far (`Rando_is_attainable`),
 * can the player actually reach the thing sitting at `location id` and pick it up? The randomizer's whole
 * placement loop is driven by this one 193-case switch.
 *
 * A location id is `<rm name> + <rm item num>` (`_WestA_2C01`), or one of the pseudo-ids the routing logic
 * leans on: a dungeon name (`STR_Parapa_Palace` = "can the player stand in front of that palace"), a town
 * name, a spell room (`<rm name> + STR_Spell`), or a skill (`STR_STABDOWN` / `STR_STABUP`).
 *
 * `*item exception` (`_ITEM_ID`) is the item that would go here: a few spots need the item to have gravity
 * (anything but `STR_RFAIRY`) or to be collectable with a stab (`STR_KEY` / `STR_PBAG`).
 *
 * Ported from `Rando_is_qual_location.gml` (3505 lines) and `Rando_is_qual_location_1a.gml` (179 lines).
 * The switch keeps ZALiA's case order and case keys verbatim.
 *
 * PORT DEVIATIONS
 * - RECURSION GUARD (port-only). `Rando_is_qual_location` calls itself from ~30 case bodies (`:34`, `:123`,
 *   `:2919`, `:3124`, `:3456`, …) and indirectly through `reach.ts` (`Rando_can_reach_RutoMtnRuins`,
 *   `Rando_can_reach_CrystalHolder`, `Rando_can_get_inside_P7`) with no guard whatsoever in ZALiA — a
 *   town/dungeon shuffle in `dm_save_data` that happened to close a loop would hang generation. The port
 *   splits the script: the exported `Rando_is_qual_location` is a guard wrapper around the module-private
 *   `qualLocationBody`. Re-entering a location id already on the stack (`self.qualStack`) or nesting deeper
 *   than `QUAL_DEPTH_LIMIT` (`self.qualDepth`) returns `false` and `sdm()`s one warning. ZALiA's own data
 *   never trips it — the call graph is acyclic and bottoms out around depth 5.
 * - Four private helpers below (`owDungeon`, `owTown`, `hasKeys`, `spellSequenceAttainable`) each inline the
 *   exact GML expression they replace; they collapse ~80 verbatim repetitions of the same four idioms.
 *
 * DROPPED — block-commented dead code (PORTING.md rule 8), each range verified in the GML:
 * - `:948-953`   — the pre-2024/08/07 extra `STR_FAIRY` requirement on the West Saria River Waterfall PBag
 *                  (`Area_WestA+'4D'+'01'`); the room was changed so JUMP alone suffices.
 * - `:1245-1275` — a SECOND set of `Area_TownA+'61'/'63'/'65'+'01'` cases. GML LATENT BUG: duplicate case
 *                  labels for the JUMP/FAIRY/FIRE spell-room item locations. The live copies are `:1218`,
 *                  `:1228`, `:1238`; the commented ones additionally required the town's own spell.
 * - `:2947-3098` — the entire `case STR_KEY+"0101"` … `case STR_KEY+"0606"` block (28 unconditional
 *                  `return true`s). Dungeon keys are qualified by their room location ids instead.
 * - `:3469-3476` — the pre-2024/10/04 "need JUMP to reach the Great Palace roof" branch in `STR_STABDOWN`.
 * Also dropped: the commented-out `case val(g.dm_rm[?STR_Spell+STR_Scene+…])` alternates that sit above the
 * spell-room cases (`:1217`, `:1227`, `:1237`, `:3122`, `:3131`, …) and `:302`'s `//case Area_DthMt+'0D'`.
 *
 * `required_spell = 0` at the top of the GML is kept: nothing in the script ever writes it back, and no
 * caller reads it (see `Rando.ts`), but the assignment is part of the observable instance state.
 */
